// TEST: Display Emit Escapes
// ============================================================================
// A `text/*` mime infers `encoding: "utf8"`, so the payload travels as a
// QUOTED JSON string and has to be escaped. Embedded quotes are the case a
// naive concatenation gets wrong, and getting it wrong is invisible in one
// lane alone -- so this file exists mainly to be run down BOTH lanes by
// `blade test interp`, where Blade.Display.Frame.escape and its generated C++
// mirror have to produce identical bytes. The full escape table (control
// characters, backslash, the sentinel's own SOH) is pinned in-process in
// tests/Test_Display.fs, where the payload does not have to survive Blade's
// string lexer first.
// ============================================================================
import display as d
let msg = "he said \"hi\" then left"
let ok = d.emit("text/plain", msg)
// EXPECT: ok = true
